FINAL EVIDENCE AND LEDGER CHECK
For each NO, start that score's reasoning with the removed-side span ID and
a SHORT verbatim quotation copied from THAT displayed span. Use about 3-8
contiguous words (or a short literal phrase in that language), without ellipses,
rewriting, or stitching together adjacent spans. A full sentence may cross the
220-character chunk boundary and is then not a quote from the cited span. Choose
a shorter visible phrase touching the actual difference, then explain the full
lost claim separately. Do not quote an entire category paragraph or rely on a
second citation's quote to validate the first citation.
The own_side_core block marks exactly which text belongs to that difference.
Check the ID on the actual fragment, not the first chunk of its paragraph. A
clause completed in the next chunk must cite that next chunk if quoted there.
Each literal citation opener is a copyable ID and short source quote. For a NO,
copy an opener from the chosen removed-side span, then explain the uncovered
meaning in context. The opener is only a literal-copy aid: it does not assert
that its span is a material loss. Do not select harmless UI as loss evidence.
Before submitting, reconcile the delta ledger with the two direction scores:
- a_can_replace_b=NO for B's useful addition requires a material span_b_delta.
- b_can_replace_a=NO for A's useful addition requires a material span_a_delta.
An explicit added email-consent condition is material_non_main_message_change,
not universal_ui_or_repetition just because it is beside a contact form.
Only a genuinely harmless/covered difference receives a covered delta.
If the whole text of one side survives, do not reject that covering direction
for an empty heading, settings pointer or ordinary banner label.
